                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b27d4001-69ab-346a-b558-580643d7a2c2",
                        "entry_id": "5f57a562-d5a4-323f-af86-5dad82c30a6c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A squat, rounded form of oenochoe with a trefoil mouth."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "475ecf08-b3bc-3c40-a2a6-256d8e36d517",
                        "entry_id": "5f57a562-d5a4-323f-af86-5dad82c30a6c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An Ancient Greek unit of liquid measure correspondent to 12 cotylae."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce5e80e1-7b6e-4684-8e81-cfb4c9dc56e8",
                                "sense_id": "475ecf08-b3bc-3c40-a2a6-256d8e36d517",
                                "text": "It follows that the seah must equal the urna, and the hin equal 2 Attic choes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c7aa95da-6f77-4f48-9433-537ed463b10d",
                                "sense_id": "475ecf08-b3bc-3c40-a2a6-256d8e36d517",
                                "text": "Accordingly one Amphoreus Metrétés contained 12 Choes, 144 Kotyloi, 864 Kyathoi. The Amphoreus held 39·39 litres or 69·33 pints, or slightly over 8½ gallons. It may generally be assumed that the great pointed pottery jars in which wines were preserved, exported and sold were, each of them, such an amphoreus."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "722ea745-1a32-4b13-aa13-42ebb8c75a6c",
                                "sense_id": "475ecf08-b3bc-3c40-a2a6-256d8e36d517",
                                "text": "Amphoreis of wine [- - -] : 590, three choes¹² […] 12. I.e., 590 amphoreis (a unit of measurement probably equivalent to 12 choes) + three choes = 7,083 choes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3de6f573-794d-4d38-853f-6f46ae91f9ce",
                                "sense_id": "475ecf08-b3bc-3c40-a2a6-256d8e36d517",
                                "text": "[…] a jar, of two metretai; a bronze jug, of four choes, and spouted cup; a tray for cups, and a second one; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d27e6a2a-b44f-449b-a107-e218cd127d8f",
                                "sense_id": "475ecf08-b3bc-3c40-a2a6-256d8e36d517",
                                "text": "The amounts are significant: 8 choes of wine equals 6 gallons; a medimnos equals 48 khoinikes. A single khoinix was a day’s grain ration for a man in Athens."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
